Luma's breakdown of the three independent invariants—Action Slot Identity, Generation State, and Turn Identity—is spot on. Combining the Action Slot transition (BUSY → DONE) with the Turn Response stabilization provides the dual-evidence completion boundary we need.
Below is the structural breakdown evaluated directly against the empirical DOM data from PP13–16, QS 9.7 telemetry, and project artifacts.
Classification Key
[A] Directly demonstrated by inspected code / PP diagnostic dumps.
[B] Engineering deduction from structural evidence.
[C] Speculation / needs live DOM run.
1. Composer Root & Action Slot Structural Anchors
ChatGPT (GPT)
Composer Root [A]: The content-editable / textarea wrapper <form> or div#composer-background container. It encapsulates both the content-editable input (#prompt-textarea) and the submit controls.
Action Slot [A]: The right-aligned control wrapper inside the form: [data-testid="send-button"] (or its direct parent div container in the footer flexbox).
Structural Identification without Labels [B]: Yes. Rather than querying aria-label="Stop answering", the adapter anchors the parent div housing the submit/voice slot. During generation, GPT unmounts the <button data-testid="send-button"> and mounts a <button data-testid="stop-button"> (or a voice/cancel node) into the exact same parent slot. Tracking the presence or attribute state of that specific slot child provides a structural signal without inspecting button text.
Claude / Chron
Composer Root [A]: The main input container card (fieldset or div wrapper around the ProseMirror editor / contenteditable field).
Action Slot [A]: The action button region positioned at the bottom right of the composer card.
Structural Identification without Labels [B]: Yes. Chron's action region toggles between an active send arrow button and a stop/pause generation control. The structural parent remains constant within the form card while the action child transitions.
2. Response Container & Noise Isolation
GPT
Response Container [A]: The primary conversation list container (div[data-message-author-role="assistant"] wrappers inside the main thread scroll container).
Noise Separation [B]: Isolate response content by binding directly to .markdown or div[data-message-author-role="assistant"] .aria-label text blocks, ignoring sibling UI elements like source drawers or copy/thumbs-up action bars.
Chron
Response Container [A]: The message turn container (div.font-claude-message or div[data-is-streaming]).
Noise Separation (Filtering "Retrieved 3 sources") [A]: The "Retrieved X sources" and artifact tool-use blocks are rendered in separate collapsible accordion DOM nodes (div.grid or div[data-test-render-count]) above or outside the primary prose block.
Fix [B]: The Chron adapter must target the prose content wrapper (.prose / div.font-claude-message) specifically, rather than taking innerText of the top-level turn container which sweeps up tool-call metadata.
3. Turn Identity Baseline (Pre-SEND Snapshot)
To prove a harvested response belongs to turn T, PP records a pre-SEND baseline containing:
Baseline Signature T
pre
​
